# Toolchain & Project Structure

## Language

**C11** (`-std=c11`). **No C++.**

## Compiler flags (from `Makefile`)

```
-std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror
-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L
-D_FILE_OFFSET_BITS=64
-Iinclude
-O2          # release (CFLAGS)
```

When the `<io.h>` / `_setmode` probe succeeds, the Makefile also adds:

```
-DTAIL_TOTO_WIN32_IO   # O_BINARY on open(), _setmode() on stdin/stdout
```

No extra libraries are linked on either platform.

Debug target uses `CFLAGS_DEBUG`: `-g -O1 -fsanitize=address,undefined -fno-omit-frame-pointer`.

## Artefact layout

All build outputs live under **`build/`**; never write binaries at the repo root
or into `tests/`.

| Artefact | Path |
|----------|------|
| Release binary | `build/tail-toto` (`.exe` on Windows) |
| Debug binary | `build/tail-toto-debug` |
| Main objects | `build/*.o` (from `src/*.c`) |
| Test binary | `build/tests/test_core` |
| Test objects | `build/tests/*.o` (from `tests/*.c`) |

`build/.gitkeep` and `build/tests/.gitkeep` keep the directories in git when empty.
`make clean` removes objects and binaries but leaves the `.gitkeep` files.

## Compiler selection

`Makefile` picks **gcc** if available, else **clang**:

```makefile
CC := $(shell command -v gcc >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo gcc || echo clang)
```

On **`OS=Windows_NT`**, if `C:/msys64/ucrt64/bin/gcc` exists, it becomes `CC`
(so Git Bash does not use a minimal or mismatched MinGW toolchain).

## Platform probe (`<io.h>`)

Before compiling, the Makefile compiles a tiny program that includes `<io.h>`
and `<fcntl.h>` and calls `_setmode(0, _O_BINARY)`:

- **Probe fails** → POSIX I/O only; full unit tests.
- **Probe succeeds** → `-DTAIL_TOTO_WIN32_IO`; stdin/stdout switched to binary
  mode and files opened with `O_BINARY` so CRLF bytes are never translated;
  pipe tests `SKIP`.

Typical outcomes:

| Environment | Probe | I/O mode |
|-------------|-------|----------|
| Linux / WSL | fail | POSIX |
| MSYS2 UCRT64 gcc | success | Win32 binary mode |
| Git Bash + UCRT64 gcc | success | Win32 binary mode |
| Cygwin / MSYS (POSIX runtime) | fail* | POSIX |

\*If a Cygwin-like runtime does pass the probe, forcing binary mode is harmless.

## Build system

**GNU Make** at repo root. Object files are compiled into `build/` and
`build/tests/`, then linked.

| Target | Output |
|--------|--------|
| `make` / `all` | `build/tail-toto` |
| `make debug` | `build/tail-toto-debug` |
| `make test` | builds + runs `build/tests/test_core` |
| `make clean` | removes objects/binaries under `build/` (keeps `.gitkeep`) |
| `make install` | `install -m 755 build/tail-toto /usr/local/bin` (Linux/macOS) |

**Main sources:** `src/main.c`, `src/tail_toto_emit.c`, `src/tail_toto_cli.c`, `src/tail_toto_io.c`, `src/tail_toto_tail.c`, `src/tail_toto_run.c`

**Test sources:** `tests/test_runner.c`, `tests/test_util.c`, `tests/test_count_parse.c`, `tests/test_lines_last.c`, `tests/test_lines_from.c`, `tests/test_bytes_last.c`, `tests/test_stream.c`

## Dependencies

- **POSIX builds:** libc only (`unistd.h`, `fcntl.h`, `sys/stat.h`, `inttypes.h`, etc.).
- **Win32 I/O builds:** libc only (UCRT `io.h` / `fcntl.h` for `_setmode`, `O_BINARY`).

