## Building on Linux / WSL

```sh
make clean && make && make test
./build/tail-toto /etc/passwd
```

## Building on Windows

**Recommended:** MSYS2 **UCRT64** or **Git Bash** with UCRT64 `gcc` on `PATH`:

```sh
pacman -S make mingw-w64-ucrt-x86_64-gcc   # once
cd /path/to/tail-toto
make clean && make && make test
./build/tail-toto README.md
```

Produces a **native Windows executable** (`build/tail-toto` or
`build/tail-toto.exe`). Runs in UCRT64, Git Bash, cmd, and PowerShell.

### Git Bash caveat

Put **`/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin` early on `PATH`** (before Git's embedded
MinGW). Otherwise `make` may pick a compiler with a different runtime (wrong
probe result, text-mode CRLF translation) or fail opaquely. Prefer:

```bash
PATH="/c/msys64/ucrt64/bin:$PATH" make
```

## Linking notes

- `main()` lives only in `src/main.c`.
- Tests link every `src/*.c` object **except `src/main.c`**; `test_runner.c`
  provides the test `main()`.
- Debug binary is compiled from sources with `CFLAGS_DEBUG` (not reused release `.o` files).
